(Bug #59 over a list widened by a `value`. A `value` carries its runtime
 tag alongside its payload (LANGUAGE.md:2489-2493), so the slot it lands
 in is tagged text - and the `treating` clause must read that tag rather
 than the loop variable's absent static type.)

a value called label is "a".
a list called items is [1, label].
print each item from items treating "a" as "b".

(The same list with a number match that matches nothing: every element
 comes through unchanged.)
print each item from items treating 98 as 31.
